  "spiritual_reading": "\n\n\n#\n Spiritual\n Translation\n\n\n---\n\n\n**\n¶2.\n** The first\n liberation\n and recovery\n pert\nains to the\n prim\nordial celestial will.\n When the celest\nial will was freed from captivity under\n the dominion of the\n self-derived\n loves\n by\n the divine rational principle proceeding from the\n Lord —\n who\n came\n forth\n on\n behalf\n of that\n celest\nial will — vast\n wisdom\n and vast\n spiritual\n pot\nency were recovered\n from the entire\n domin\nion of self-love. These\n asc\nended together\n with the celestial will into\n the interior\n heav\nenly\n states.\n This is the first recovery\n.\n\n**¶3.**\n The second recovery\n pertains to the divine\n rational principle. When the Divine\n Good as\n origin\n and the Divine Truth as origin together\n established the ordered degrees of the mind and\n all\n its\n interior\n and\n exterior states\n,\n and\n arranged\n the natural\n planes\n of\n thought\n together\n with the ruling\n loves\n that\n govern them\n, imm\neasurable wisdom\n was recovered from\n those\n states\n —\n wisdom belonging\n to the celest\nial will that\n had been consumed and\n absorbed by the prop\nrium...\n\n\n**¶4.** \n*(\nThe\n text\n is\n too\n fragmentary for confident\n translation.\n What\n remains\n suggests three\n states\n of spiritual temptation-combat occurring\n across\n time\n,\n with a\n power\n operating\n from\n above\n upon\n the whole\n organized\n form\n of the mind.)*\n\n**\n¶5.** The third recovery pert\nains to Divine\n Truth manifesting in a further\n degree of\n accommodation\n. It\n presented\n its intellig\nible form —\n the visible\n shape\n of wisdom\n — before\n the mind\n,\n confront\ning the domin\nion of self-love,\n and recovered\n from\n that dominion what\n belonged\n to it\n. Thus\n the intellig\nible form of wisdom appeared\n within\n this\n third degree of the\n divine\n proce\neding.\n\n\n**¶6.** The\n fourth recovery pertains to Divine\n Truth in its fullness of\n rad\niance. When\n it was revealed within\n the sphere\n of spiritual life, it presented\n the\n form of divine wisdom before the rational\n faculty\n and\n pur\nified the interior\n wisdom that ab\nides\n above the\n rational\n.\n It\n gr\nounded the first state\n of genuine good. It took\n on\n the likeness of heav\nenly affections,\n making\n itself like them\n in\n their\n degree\n,\n until\n it traveled\n down\nward and descended into the natural and sens\nual plane\n of\n the mind. It set in order the\n natural\n states of thought\n and all\n the bonds that\n held\n them\n fixed\n. It also\n loosened wisdom\n beyond\n measure throughout the entire organized\n structure\n of the mind. It im\nparted the call of truth and the\n capacity for willing\n reception to all\n the basic faculties,\n and it\n brought\n forth the\n regenerated natural understanding.\n Then\n it ascended and came\n to rest in\n the celest\nial heaven.\n\n**¶7\n.** The fifth liberation\n and recovery pertains to the great operation\n of\n divine providence —\n which\n is the calling\n of\n divine truth and the willing reception of\n it\n —\n for\n this\n operation\n also bears\n the\n interior\n spiritual life forth\n from the celestial kingdom into\n the lower\n degrees.\n\n\n**¶8.** \n*(Much\n is\n lost\n.\n What\n remains traces\n a\n sequence\n:\n)\n*\n The divine\n rational principle im\nparts the successive\n stages\n of liberation\n.\n In\n the first stage\n, there\n is asc\nent...\n accompanied\n by wisdom\n... In\n the fourth\n stage, wisdom\n operates\n in\n its\n own\n degree... And in the fifth,\n wisdom\n enters\n into the\n ou\ntermost natural\n form\n,\n sets\n it\n in order, and imp\nresses\n its\n lumin\nous image upon the\n final\n external form of the regenerated person —\n the Last Statue —\n which\n is the ultimate\n natural\n expression\n of all\n that\n has\n been in\nwardly recovered.\n\n**¶\n9.** These\n five essential\n divine\n operations were made\n manifest\n. They came forth\n into\n spiritual\n use and\n were established upon successive\n degrees.\n The celest\nial will,\n when\n it came forth\n from\n tem\nptation-combat, set\n in order and\n constructed the whole\n organized\n form of the mind. All\n proceeds\n from the\n celest\nial will and\n its coming into the\n world\n.\n\n\n**\n¶10.** In this manner\n these\n operations\n persist\n together\n within\n the mind...\n\n\n**¶11.** ...\non\n account\n of the wisdom\n that had rushed forth\n from the divine\n truth\n in its\n accommod\nated manifest\nation.",
  "reconstructions": [
    {
      "paragraph": 2,
      "reconstructed_text": "[The first loo]sening and saving is that of [the] First Man, since when the First M[a]n was freed fro[m the prison of] the rulers by the Living Spirit, who had come [down on account] of the First Man, much light and [much] power was saved from the entire ruling-power. They ascended with the First Man to the aeons [of] greatn[ess]. This [is the first] release."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 7,
      "reconstructed_text": "The fifth release and saving is that of the great counsel, w[hich is the s]umm[ons an]d the obedience, since it also [sends forth] the soul from the [land] of greatness."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 8,
      "reconstructed_text": "[So also] the Living Spirit [gave each one,] as he gave [them] the release [in their order.] The first [is the one where he] ascended and he [brought forth light,] as he [gathered] wisdom [from the darkness.] The fourth [bestows upon it] its wisdom [in its own degree.] And also, the fifth [enters] into it, and it sets it in order [and impresses] its light image in this Last Statue."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 9,
      "reconstructed_text": "These five grea[t] powe[rs of light] were revealed. They came to a profit [and a saving;] they were established upon [their degrees. The] First Man [came first, for] when he came toward [the height] from the struggle. He set in order and constructed [the whole] universe [. All things proceed from] the First M[an and] his advent."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 10,
      "reconstructed_text": "In [t]his way [also] they st[an]d with [one another.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 11,
      "reconstructed_text": "[This was] because of the light [th]at had rushed from [the image of] the Amba[s]sa[d]or."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 5,
      "reconstructed_text": "[\nThe third red]emption is that\n of the Thi[rd Ambassador\n, since when he] displayed [his\n image before the firmaments,] he\n [shook and cast down the r\n]uling-power; he [\nreleased much light] from them [through\n his image.] So this is [\nhow] the [power of] his\n image that [was revealed] in the\n Th[ir]d Ambassador."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 3,
      "reconstructed_text": "The second saving is that of the Liv[ing] Spirit, since whe[n] the Father of Life and [the] Mother of [Li]fe constructed [the ... ...] and [w]orlds [... wo]rlds, the earths and their [rulers; im]measurable light was saved f[r]om them [... the First] Man, who w[a]s devoured [...] lig[ht [ ... ]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 4,
      "reconstructed_text": "[ ... ] [ ... ] th]ree wars [... ...] to the time when he [... ...] above [...] them upon the [... ...] universe."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 6,
      "reconstructed_text": "[Th]e fourth s[av]ing is that of Jesus the Splendour, since whe[n he was] re[ve]aled in the zone he displayed [his im]age in front of the firmaments and purified [the light] that is above. He established the first righteous o[ne ...] . He took the likeness [...] he made himself like the angels in [...] un[til] he travelled and descended to the form of flesh. He set in order [t]he earths and all the fastenings. He also loosen[ed ...] light without measure in the entire structure. He gave [the] summons and the obedience to the elements, he formed [J]esus the Youth. He as[ce]n[d]ed and rested himself in the light [land]."
    }
  ],
